# Inactive identity integration partition constructors

This preparation adds unsigned physical-root constructors; it installs no plan, lock or snapshot.
The live completion contract remains 1.0.11; actual 1.0.12 adoption is a separate required step.

The APIs bind historical source origins, current inputs, byte budgets and fresh output ownership.
Normative production requires admitted catalogue and policy bindings; defaults refuse pending hooks.
Emission rechecks a private immutable readset and rejects changed metadata, bindings and source bytes.

The suite retains 20 constructor cases and all 19 prior derive/guard cases in normal and optimized modes.
Staged 799-unit fixtures exercise constructor behavior; they are not actual generator or adoption results.
Raw execution receipts and test streams identify which commands ran and their exact source inputs.

The complete unexecuted first candidate and both integrity findings remain retained as evidence.
CI separates constructor cases from the existing plan job while preserving every existing case.
Inclusive source is 399 production / 789 authored lines, including 18 CI changes and 20 publication lines.

Native, library, SQL/HTTP/UI, backend restart, capacity and full SysON feature acceptance remain open.
